  "security_implications": "in_process indicates whether the HMAC engine is busy. Incorrect in_process state (e.g., cleared prematurely while sensitive data is still being processed, or stuck high blocking completion) could leak intermediate digest values, expose key material, or allow unauthorized access to hash state. The mutual-exclusion assumption on reg_hash_stop and reg_hash_done is critical to avoid priority-induced misbehavior that could violate security guarantees.",
